-- title:
--   The signed Type I estimate from the initial half-block bound
-- statement:
--   Assume the specified uniform initial half-block bound. For $q\ge4$, $(|a|,q)=1$, $4\alpha=a/q+\beta$, and $|\beta|\le q^{-2}$, let $40\le U,V<x$, $UV\le x/4$, and $x\le UV^2$. Then
--   $$|T_I|\le\frac{x}{2q}\log x\log(2UV/q+4)+0.89\left(UV+\frac52q\right)(8+\log q)\log(2x).$$
--   The initial half-block estimate remains an explicit hypothesis of this intermediate lemma.
-- source:
--   Terence Tao, Every odd number greater than 1 is the sum of at most five primes, https://arxiv.org/abs/1201.6656, Sections 5 and 6. Original Lean source: Theorems/Thm_TaoFivePrimes_vaughan_typeI_ordinary_final_assembly.lean, lines 409-427.

